From d4f15199b89aae84a4d1dad34aa1820b84b9e156 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:34:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/vc4: time HDMI stereo rasters throughout the display
 pipeline

vc4 advertises HDMI stereo modes but still programs a one-view raster.
After group34 selects the whole-frame TMDS rate this also disagrees with
the clock programmed by the common HDMI state helper.

Expand CRTC timing with the common helper and connector SBS-full flags,
then use it for PV and HDMI registers, whole-frame HVS dimensions and
load. Preserve the logical mode for AVI/VSIF. Use negotiated stereo TMDS
for scrambling and audio CTS. Keep ordinary 2D timing behavior.

Validate layout, interlace, overflow and generation register bounds before
common HDMI math. Reject packed-raster overscan, field alternative and
interlaced frame packing until their DE/sync sequences are implemented.

Add KUnit coverage invoking the actual encoder check, with fixed CEA/spec
expectations, both SBS-full choices, repeated checks, VIC preservation,
RGB8/RGB12 rate agreement, DBLCLK and invalid-mode negative controls.
The original 22 rows fail 18 times before the fix. The extended 44 rows
and all 33 existing vc4 rows pass under ARM64 QEMU. This is no physical
Pi or HDMI link qualification.

Assisted-by: gpt-6-astra via Codex
